# Files excluded from a Vercel deployment.
#
# Deployments made through the GitHub integration only contain committed
# files, and .gitignore already keeps the large data directories out of the
# repository. A `vercel` CLI deploy works from the working directory instead,
# where Input/, history/ and updating_files/ are present and total ~450 MB.
# Without this file every CLI deploy would upload all of it.

# --- secrets: never upload, never in the bundle ---
# Patterns without a slash match at any depth, so `.env.*` also covers
# liveapp/.env - the negation keeps the committed template.
.env
.env.*
liveapp/.env
liveapp/seed_users.json
!liveapp/.env.example

# --- source data and ETL outputs: build machine only ---
Input/
output/
history/
updating_files/
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.parquet
*.zip
liveapp/storage/

# --- local Python artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- tooling / docs: not needed at runtime ---
.git/
.gitignore
.venv
DEPLOYMENT.md
LIVE_DATABASE_DASHBOARD.md
PROCESS_SUMMARY.md
liveapp/README.md

# --- ETL scripts: run on the build machine, never inside the function ---
Rename.py
achieved_sbf.py
find_easy_sbf.py
find_opening_easy_sbf.py
monthly_reset.py
zip_site.py
publish_site.py

# KEEP: liveapp/** (app + frontend), _dashboard_template.html, api/**, build_dashboard.py